This is a solver-shape control, not an authentic E. coli, glycerol, or Shewanella configuration. It has 100 real-valued variables and 140 random three-variable rows, constructed around a satisfying witness. Variables use [0, 8] bounds; 25 are deliberately unbounded. Each row is relaxed to the band -1 <= row <= 1. The weighted objective has a lower bound attained by the constructed witness. The random seed is 0.

Variant: free25-bound-tol1. This deliberately preserves one of the four generic solver-shape controls from the original SyntheticFBA proposal and is included only under the plain profile.
Numeric profile: legacy solver control with flux upper bound 8.

This file is a structural floating-point translation of that source instance. Real variables are replaced by (_ FloatingPoint 15 113) variables. Real arithmetic is replaced by roundNearestTiesToEven floating-point arithmetic, and numeric constants are pre-rounded once to exact target-format literals. Linear comparisons become floating-point comparisons; equality uses IEEE fp.eq. No finite-value guards are added.

Floating point is not the reals; satisfiability is not assumed to survive this translation. The translated status is unknown.

